# Snowflake Integration Rules

## 🔐 CORE PRINCIPLES
- **SSH KEY ONLY**: JWT auth - NO password allowed
- **READ-ONLY**: Only SELECT/WITH queries
- **SERVER-SIDE ONLY**: Never in client components
- **MEMORY SAFE**: Connection tracking + auto-cleanup

## 📋 CONFIGURATION

### AWS Secrets Manager (required)
```json
{
  "SNOWFLAKE_USER": "SERVICE_USER", 
  "SNOWFLAKE_SSH_KEY": "-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...",
  "SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT": "vya01839.us-east-1",
  "SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE": "COMPUTE_WH",
  "SNOWFLAKE_ROLE": "READER"
}
```

### App Config (not in secrets)
```typescript
const SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE = 'ANALYTICS_DB';
const SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA = 'PUBLIC';
```

## 📁 FILE STRUCTURE
```
src/lib/secrets/snowflake.ts              # Config from secrets
src/lib/connections/connection-manager.ts # Memory leak prevention
src/lib/connections/base-connection.ts    # Connection wrapper
src/lib/services/snowflake-service.ts     # Query execution
src/app/api/snowflake/query/route.ts      # POST query, GET test
